      "writtenOn": "2024-06-07T08:04:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still prefer a crash, that increasing the timeout.\n\nIf the timeout is increase to 2, then if there are a crash we will increase it to 3, if there is no crash but a too long cleanup, we will just freeze some operation for that long and the quality of the code is only going down.\n\nIf we have a crash, we can monitor it and potentially have a bugreport / logs that help fixing it.\n\nAnother reason to not increase this timer is that there are other component that may be relying on the cleanup being done in 1 second. I am thinking on android of the systemServer, in case we are switching user, that has a few time constrain to relaunch a Bluetooth process for the new user. But there will be a few other scenario. I am sure ChromeOs will have some scenario too",
      "parentUuid": "ce83fa24_e57a1415",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "b4191ba199c1255bfddc6a352344a10e211278bc",
